---
import TechniquePost from "../../layouts/TechniquePost.astro"
import TooltipBuild from "../../components/UnderTheHood/TooltipBuild.astro"
import Code from "../../components/Code.astro"
---

<TechniquePost slug="tooltip-interest-invokers">
  <section>
    <h2 id="the-problem">The problem</h2>
    <p>
      A tooltip opens on hover and focus, closes on <kbd>Esc</kbd>, blur and
      leave, and stays next to its trigger without running off the screen. Every
      part of that used to be JavaScript: event listeners, delays and a
      positioning library that measures and flips.
    </p>
    <p>Now it's two attributes and a few lines of CSS.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="the-trick">The trick</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>interestfor</code> on the trigger and <code>popover="hint"</code> on
        the tooltip: it opens on hover and focus, no JavaScript
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>commandfor</code> with <code>command="toggle-popover"</code> opens it
        on tap, where there is no hover
      </li>
      <li>
        The invoker becomes the implicit anchor: no <code>anchor-name</code>, no
        ids to wire up in CSS
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>position-area: block-start</code> centers it above the trigger
      </li>
    </ul>
    <Code
      lang="html"
      code={`<button
  type="button"
  interestfor="tooltip"
  commandfor="tooltip"
  command="toggle-popover"
>
  Save
</button>

<span class="tooltip" id="tooltip" popover="hint">Save changes</span>`}
    />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="staying-on-screen">Staying on screen</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>position-try-fallbacks</code> flips the tooltip below the trigger when
        there's no room above
      </li>
      <li>
        Two <code>@position-try</code> rules use <code>anchor-size(inline)</code
        > to slide it sideways at the edge of the window, still over the trigger
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>position-visibility: anchors-visible</code> hides it when the trigger
        scrolls out of view
      </li>
      <li>
        An arrow follows along: the tooltip is its own anchor, and <code
          >clamp()</code
        > keeps the arrow on its edge, as close to the trigger as it gets
      </li>
      <li>
        Near an edge, <code>calc-size(max-content, min(size, 10rem))</code> keeps
        long text at least <code>10rem</code> wide, while short labels stay snug
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="try-it">Try it</h2>
    <TooltipBuild />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="fallback">Fallback</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Without interest invokers, hover and focus do nothing, and <code
          >commandfor</code
        > still toggles the tooltip on click
      </li>
      <li>
        An unknown <code>popover</code> value falls back to <code>manual</code>,
        so the tooltip stays open until it's toggled again
      </li>
      <li>
        There's no <code>@supports</code> fallback for anchor positioning or <code
          >calc-size()</code
        >: those declarations are ignored, and the tooltip isn't placed next to
        its trigger
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</TechniquePost>
